FUN_1000_184b: MEMMGR driver/scratch-struct allocator — faithful dynamic-segment reconstruction.

184b is the MEMMGR object allocator reached via the DIRECT path (FUN_0000_14da -> FUN_1000_182a, struct
DGROUP:0x4f0 scratch), via the driver method vector DGROUP:0xd0 (from FUN_1000_5051, struct 0x3e4 video /
0x4fa sound), and via the descriptor-pool refill (FUN_1000_161d -> 17e5, struct DGROUP:0x1738). The struct
lives at CX:BX where CX (param_2) = the DGROUP segment (ds=DGROUP=0x1c00 at runtime; the decompile
sometimes captured the static SS placeholder 0x2ba9) and BX (param_4) is the near offset. asm 0x1184b:

    mov es,cx                 ; ES = DGROUP
    or  byte es:[bx+2],0x22   ; struct[+2] flags |= 0x22        <-- SIGSEGV when base dropped (*0x4f2)
    js  .flag                 ; bit7 branch (1345/0d70); not taken on the boot alloc path
    mov bp,0x16d4 ; mov [bp+0x1e],bx   ; SS:0x16f2 = struct offset (SS=DGROUP; Ghidra used static SS 0x2ba9)
    call 0a31                 ; the free-list allocator; returns AX = the allocated segment and leaves
                              ;   ES = the descriptor node it carved (g_mm_es)
    jb  .err
    mov es:[6],bx ; mov es:[8],cx      ; descriptor[6]/[8] = struct off / DGROUP (owner back-ptr)
    mov ds,cx ; mov ax,es:[0] ; mov [bx],ax   ; struct[0] = descriptor.base = the allocated segment (=load_seg)
    mov ax,0xa0 ; mov [bx+2],ax ; mov es:[2],ax ; struct[2]=0xa0, descriptor[2]=0xa0
    mov ax,es ; lret          ; returns AX = descriptor seg

Ghidra dropped the ES=CX/DS=CX segment bases on every struct access (rendered the bare offset as a host
pointer -> SIGSEGV), mis-based the SS slot store (DAT_2000_d182 @ 0x2d182 instead of DGROUP:0x16f2), and —
because it folded 0a31's node-walking DS to the DGROUP context — mis-read the allocated segment from
DGROUP:0 (DAT_1000_c000) instead of the descriptor node ES:[0] that 0a31 actually returns. Fix (paired with
patch 025's faithful 0a31): base every struct access at g_mem+(0x1c00<<4)+(uint16_t)param_4; take the CF
from the shared g_mm_cf and ES (the descriptor) from g_mm_es that 0a31 exposes; struct[0] = 0a31's return
(= descriptor.base = the allocated segment). Asm-verified base-0 0x1184b..0x118a3.
